      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Headaches due to endocrine diseases in childhood are rare, but any child with chronic headaches should be given serious consideration. The most serious etiology is a tumor of the hypothalamic-pituitary region. Headaches can also occur as premenstrual migraine or as water retention due to glucocorticoid or Growth Hormone (GH) overdosage."},
